# AppModal — mandatory modal shell

When creating or editing a **center dialog** in the SPA:

1. Use `AppModal` from `app/src/app/components/AppModal.tsx`
2. Structure with `AppModalHeader`, `AppModalBody`, and `AppModalFooter` (footer optional for single-button forms)
3. Read `_System_Core/005_SPA_UX_Patterns.md` § Modal patterns for the canonical recipe

## Required props

- `open` + `onClose` — backdrop click closes via motion button
- `labelledBy` + `titleId` on header — accessibility
- `panelClassName` — width only (`max-w-md w-full`, etc.); do not override backdrop/panel base styles

## Do not

- Add new `fixed inset-0` dialog overlays in pages or components
- Duplicate backdrop (`bg-black/40`) or card shell classes — use exported `appModalBackdropClass` / `appModalPanelClass` if needed outside the component
- Invent a new modal animation — `AppModal` already uses `useReducedMotion()` + `appModalSpring`

## Allowed alternatives

| Case | Use |
|------|-----|
| POS tiles / checkout | `POSModal` in `posMotion.tsx` |
| CSR alias (backward compat) | `FulfillmentModal` (= re-export of `AppModal`) |
| Radix confirm | `AlertDialog` from `ui/alert-dialog.tsx` |
| Side drawer / sheet | `BatchTraceabilityDrawer`, `Sheet`, `Drawer` |

## New feature modals

Extract a named component (e.g. `DeliveryReviewEditModal.tsx`) that composes `AppModal` — do not leave modal JSX inline in page files unless trivial one-off (&lt;10 lines).
